      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'm not able to give you a diagnosis, but what you're describing—heart palpitations with dizziness—is worth mentioning to a doctor, especially since it's happening repeatedly. Caffeine can absolutely cause heart flutters, so cutting back on coffee is a reasonable first step. That said, if you experience chest pain, fainting, severe shortness of breath, or the episodes last longer or get more intense, seek medical care promptly. It's always better to get heart symptoms checked out, even if they turn out to be benign.",
